# An account, as the `accounts` table stores it: the name its holder signs
# with, a digest of the password, the address its mail goes to, when that
# address was confirmed, and what a sign-in counts. The password itself is
# never stored. This module is named for the record, so the models
# derivation declares `account` here with a field for each column.
#
# Anyone may make an account.
pub fn create? _ _
  true

# Its holder may change it, which is how a password is changed. What the
# app keeps on its own account (the count of wrong passwords, the lock, the
# confirmation) it writes as the app.
pub fn update? viewer a
  viewer == a.name
